  "description": "The IPFS copy of a consent document, fetched from a list of gateways in order (each a prefix to which the CID is appended, or a template carrying {cid}). The default list is defaultGateways; ipfsGateways replaces it; ipfsGateway, a gateway the user names, is asked first, before the list. A gateway is trusted for nothing: its bytes count only once they re-encode to the CID (a CIDv0 is base58btc(0x12 0x20 sha256(the one dag-pb node whose UnixFS File data is the whole file)), and a body over 262144 bytes, an HTTP error, a network error or bytes that do not re-encode move to the next gateway. Bytes that re-encode are the document: the disclosure hash decides, pass or fail, and no further gateway is asked. The bundle is receipts/cidv1.bundle.json (resolver = receipts/did-documents.json, verifyDisclosure true, no rpcUrl); its document CID is `cid`, whose pinned bytes are `file`, exactly. An answer body is pinned (those bytes), html (an HTML page), other-json ({\"disclosure\":{}}) or oversize (262145 bytes of spaces); a URL with no answer is a network error. disclosureGateway is result.disclosureGateway (absent when no gateway delivered); tried lists the URLs fetched, in order.",
